.TH RAMBO 1 "2026-08-21" "rambo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rambo \- kernel-backed, policy-driven RAM monitor and OOM killer daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rambo
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rambo is an event-driven, kernel-backed system monitor for Linux. It watches
RAM (via cgroup v2 limits), temperature (hwmon), pressure (PSI), network
(netlink), CPU and disk, then acts on configurable policies: desktop
notifications, graceful SIGTERM to a score-picked process, or suspending heavy
jobs.
.PP
Detection (watchers) is separated from policy (a config-driven engine), so
adding a sensor or changing behaviour never requires touching daemon logic.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the monitor (event loop) in the foreground. This is what the systemd user
service executes.
.TP
.B top
One-shot view of system stats and top RAM consumers.
.TP
.B stats
Live dashboard (Ctrl+C to exit).
.TP
.B threshold set
Set memory thresholds and alert levels. See \fBthreshold\fR help.
.TP
.B threshold status
Show current thresholds.
.TP
.B protect add --name <name>
Protect a process name from being killed.
.TP
.B protect remove --name <name>
Remove a process name from the protect list.
.TP
.B protect list
List protected process names.
.TP
.B oom-protect
Privileged helper (via pkexec): set oom_score_adj=-1000 on protected processes.
Normally invoked automatically by the daemon; not intended for manual use.
.TP
.B history
Show past events and kills with reasons.
.TP
.B clean
Delete the log file.
.TP
.B version
Print version information.
.TP
.B completion [bash|zsh|fish|powershell]
Generate shell completion script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rambo/config.toml
Main configuration file. See \fBREADME.md\fR for all options.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/rambo/state.json
Event and kill history (last 500 records).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rambo/rambo.log
Kill log and notification fallback.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/99-rambo.rules
Polkit rule allowing passwordless \fBrambo oom-protect\fR via pkexec.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/rambo.service
Systemd user service unit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives at \fI~/.config/rambo/config.toml\fR and is created with
sensible defaults on first run. It migrates automatically from the legacy
\fIconfig.json\fR if present.
.PP
See \fBhttps://github.com/jashk120/rambo#configuration\fR for a full example.
.SH SYSTEMD
Enable and start the daemon:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user enable --now rambo.service
journalctl --user -u rambo -f
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B non-zero
Error.
